 780:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  *
 781:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  * The function PLIC_SetPriority_Threshold() sets the threshold for a particular
 782:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  * hart. The default threshold on reset is 0.
 783:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  * The PFSoC Core Complex supports setting of an interrupt priority threshold
 784:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  * via the threshold register. The threshold is a WARL field, where the PFSoC
 785:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  * Core Complex supports a maximum threshold of 7.
 786:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  * The PFSoC Core Complex will mask all PLIC interrupts of a priority less than
 787:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  * or equal to threshold. For example, a threshold value of zero permits all
 788:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  * interrupts with non-zero priority, whereas a value of 7 masks all
 789:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  * interrupts.
 790:C:\Users\Martin\Libero\fpga_labor\fpga_labor\software\dma_test\src\platform/mpfs_hal/common\mss_plic.h ****  */
